# Web SPA environment. Vite exposes only `VITE_`-prefixed vars to the app.
#
# You normally do NOT need this file: in the monorepo the API URL is derived from backend/.env
# (SERVER_HOST/SERVER_PORT) by apps/web/vite.config.ts, so changing the backend port there is enough
# and the SPA follows with zero edits here.
#
# Copy to `.env` and set VITE_API_URL ONLY to override that — e.g. a standalone SPA build/deploy
# where backend/.env is absent, or to point at a remote API. Bare host of the Laravel API: NO
# trailing slash and NO `/api` suffix (the client adds `/api/...` and hits Fortify actions at the
# root, e.g. `/login`). Use `localhost` (NOT 127.0.0.1) so the Sanctum session cookie, scoped to
# `SESSION_DOMAIN=localhost`, round-trips.
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
